er"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The show-frets type indicates whether to show tablature frets as numbers (0, 1, 2) or letters (a, b, c). The"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default choice is numbers.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLShowFrets","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLShowFrets","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/showFrets":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/showFrets","title":"showFrets","type":"topic","kind":"sy